<title>SINGAPORE: Datacraft wins China and India deals.</title>
<headline>Datacraft wins China and India deals.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telecommunications and network systems integrator Datacraft Asia Ltd said on Tuesday it had won a US$1.0 million contract to build a global communications network for a shipping company in China.</p>
<p>The China project, secured by Datacraft China, would enable cost-effective business communications services between the shipping company's branch offices and its agencies worldwide.</p>
<p>Datacraft also said it secured a deal from India's Telecom Technology Centre - Centre of Development of Telematics to set up an Asynchronous Transfer Mode (ATM) switch.</p>
<p>The deal was won by Datacraft RPG - a joint venture between Datacraft Asia and RPG Enterprises in India.</p>
<p>Datacraft would also be responsible for training and technical support of the ATM switch.</p>
